.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH UPTIME 1 "2026-09-01"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
uptime \- Display the current time, the length of time the system has been up,
the number of users on the system, and the average number of jobs
in the run queue over the last 1, 5 and 15 minutes.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBuptime\fR [OPTION]...
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Display the current time, the length of time the system has been up,
the number of users on the system, and the average number of jobs
in the run queue over the last 1, 5 and 15 minutes.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-since\fR
system up since
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-pretty\fR
show uptime in pretty format
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIpath\fR]
file to search boot time from
.SH "نسخه (VERSION)"
v(uutils coreutils) 0.11.0
